course: dictionary
lesson: 2796
title: Disposal and getting rid of things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Disposal means getting rid of something, usually in a safe way. «Waste disposal» is how rubbish is taken away and dealt with. Check the words around it: the robot sentence is about danger, so disposal means dealing safely with something risky.
explain: «A bomb-disposal robot is a tracked robot with cameras and an arm, driven by remote control, so people can stay far away from danger.» The word bomb tells you the job is dangerous, and «far away from danger» tells you why a robot does it. Try your meaning in the sentence: a bomb-getting-rid-of robot still makes sense.
explain: Be careful with «at your disposal». It does not mean throwing something away. It means you can use it whenever you want. If a helper is at your disposal, you can call on them whenever you need. Read the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Disposal means the act of getting rid of something, such as rubbish or old batteries.
fact: «At your disposal» means available for you to use whenever you want.
fact: «Bomb disposal» means getting rid of a bomb safely, and a robot can do it so people stay far away.
fact: In the US, a disposal is a machine in a kitchen sink that chops up food waste.
fact: Disposal is usually uncountable, so say «waste disposal», not «a disposal», unless you mean the sink machine.
exercise: «A bomb-disposal robot is a tracked robot with cameras and an arm, driven by remote control.» What is the robot's job? | To race across Mars | To cook food in the kitchen | *To get rid of dangerous bombs safely, so people stay far away | To tidy up the bedrooms
exercise: «The workshop has a helper at your disposal.» What does at your disposal mean? | Chopped into small pieces | Thrown away in the bin | Hidden under the stairs | *Available for you to use whenever you want
exercise: Mum says, «Take the old batteries for safe disposal.» What is safe disposal? | *Getting rid of the batteries in a safe way | Charging the batteries up again | Using the batteries to power a torch | Painting the batteries bright colours
test: Which word means getting rid of waste? | Tracked | Remote | Cameras | *Disposal
test: «The rover drives on Mars, where no person has ever stood.» What does this tell you? | *The rover goes where people should not go | The rover cooks dinner on Mars | The rover never moves | The rover is made of wood
exam: In the US, a disposal is a machine in a sink. What does it chop up? | *Food waste | Glass windows | Clean plates | Wooden spoons
